he \"first dose\" is what START TIME is: the first dose time. Picking a time sets the first dose. Then the TIMES OF DAY 7:00 AM should maybe change? Hmm.\n\nLet me test: set start time to 6:00 AM (before 7:00 AM time of day) — then preview should show today 7:00? Actually current time 6:52, 6:00 today already passed → next tomorrow. Set start time to 5:00 PM (17:00) — then first dose today at 7:00 PM? no, time of day is 7:00 AM.\n\nHmm, let me reconsider. Maybe START TIME isn't first dose; maybe it's just when the group begins. TIMES OF DAY are the scheduled doses. Preview shows next 2 doses after start datetime.\n\nLet me test the first-dose picker behavior more precisely: with night owl off, toggling? Let's first turn night owl off and see preview. Actually night owl affects dates: doses before 04:00 count as previous day. 7:00 AM isn't before 4 AM, so no effect.\n\nLet's test: set start date to a future date and see preview. Also test the reported change: picked value compared with stored one before applied. Maybe there's a bug where picking the same value fails to apply, or picking time doesn't refresh preview.\n\nLet me change START TIME from 8:00 AM back to earlier and see whether preview reverts. Actually let's try setting start time to 6:00 AM today. Then preview should be \"Tomorrow 7:00 AM\" still (since 6:00 passed but 7:00 today still future?). Hmm confusing.\n\nWait, more careful: current time shown in status bar 6:52. Start time 8:00 AM. Preview: \"7:00 AM Tomorrow\" then \"Nov 16 Mon\". If start time 8:00 is activation, then doses at 7:00 AM daily from start datetime onward → first occurrence after 8:00 AM Nov 14 is Nov 15 7:00. Correct.\n\nIf start time were \"Now\" 6:51, first occurrence after 6:51 Nov 14 is Nov 14 7:00 → \"7:00 AM Today\". Plausible.\n\nSo the system seems consistent. The bug might be elsewhere: when the picked value equals the stored value, maybe something is skipped causing e.g. preview not updating.\n\nLet's test the case: pick 