{"type": "thinking", "text": "Now start time 2:00 AM, and a hint \"After midnight\" appears. Preview shows tomorrow 7:00 AM. Hmm: start at 2:00 AM today (now 6:52 AM, so 2:00 passed), first dose 7:00 AM today should be valid (7:00 > 2:00 today). But preview shows Tomorrow! That's a bug? Wait, with night owl enabled and doses before 04:00 count as previous day... 7:00 AM isn't before 4. Hmm.\n\nWait maybe because current time is now 6:52? 7:00 today is in the future. Start 2:00 today. So first dose should be today 7:00 AM. Preview says Tomorrow 7:00 AM. Suspicious.\n\nBut when start time was 7:00 AM, preview showed Today 7:00. So start=7:00 yields today. Start=2:00 → tomorrow? That's backwards. Unless with time passed (2:00 < now 6:52), the system starts the schedule from \"now\" rather than start datetime; then today 7:00 would still be future. Hmm.\n\nHmm wait, maybe when start time < now, it moves start date to tomorrow? That'd be odd but maybe intentional: start datetime in the past → next day? Actually maybe the app clamps to future: if the start datetime is in the past, it schedules from tomorrow.\n\nBut then earlier start \"Now\" (6:51) preview showed Tomorrow at 7:00 AM even though 7:00 today was future by 9 min. Hmm wait, earlier when start was \"Now\", preview showed Tomorrow too. So start < now → first dose tomorrow? Hmm no, \"Now\" = 6:51 and 7:00 today is future, yet preview showed tomorrow. That suggests the preview logic starts from tomorrow when start <= now? But with start 7:00 (future), preview showed today 7:00.\n\nSo rule: if start datetime in past (or now), skip today's doses? That's questionable but maybe the implementation is: first dose = start datetime if start has times? Hmm.\n\nLet me think about the app's model: Group has startDate, startTime (first dose time?) and schedule with times of day. Actually maybe START TIME is the \"first dose\" — i.e., the time of the very first dose, and TIMES OF DAY are the subsequent daily times? Hmm.\n\nActually the area is \"group setup and scheduling\", so preview is important. The bug to find may be here: after picking the first-dose time, the preview or saved schedule is wrong.\n\nNotice \"After midnight\" label appears for 2:00 AM. Interesting.\n\nLet's test night owl off with start 2:00 AM. Toggle night owl off, and compare preview dates."}
