{"type": "thinking", "text": "Whoa! Toggling night owl OFF changed START DATE from \"Nov 14 Sat\" to \"Nov 15 Sun\"! That's a bug: toggling night owl mode shifted the start date by one day. Actually wait — maybe when night owl was enabled and start time 2:00 AM, the \"start date\" field displayed Nov 14 but internally it was Nov 15 (night owl means 2:00 AM belongs to previous day). Hmm, the label \"After midnight\" disappeared too when night owl off.\n\nLet me think: when night owl enabled and start datetime 2:00 AM Nov 14, the dose at 2:00 AM on Nov 14 counts as previous day (Nov 13). But the start date displayed Nov 14. After turning off, start date becomes Nov 15 Sun. That's a state shift — suspicious.\n\nHmm wait, maybe that's expected? Night owl mode: a dose at 2:00 AM on Nov 14 counts as Nov 13. So maybe when night owl is on, the start date is represented as Nov 15 to make the first dose \"Nov 14\" under night owl? Hmm, this is confusing.\n\nLet me back up and test cleanly. I should reset state. Let me cancel this group and start over to test systematically, or just carefully observe.\n\nActually, this could be the reported bug about first-dose picker: \"a picked value is now compared with the stored one before it is applied.\" Meaning when picking time 2:00 AM with night owl on, the app might silently change the start date. Hmm.\n\nLet's examine: Night owl ON, start time 2:00 AM, start date Nov 14. Preview: Tomorrow 7:00 AM, Nov 16 Mon. Toggle night owl OFF: start date becomes Nov 15 Sun, start time 2:00, preview same. That's a change in the date. Is that a bug? Possibly intended: night owl mode changes how date is displayed for after-midnight doses. But the start time 2:00 AM with date Nov 14: under night owl, 2:00 AM Nov 14 = Nov 13's dose.\n\nHmm, this could be a genuine bug where toggling night owl modifies the start date. But is it in the \"changed\" list? Night owl caption change only.\n\nLet me get back to clean state: cancel group creation and start over? Actually data hasn't been saved so cancel is safe. But I'd like to test more.\n\nLet me re-enable night owl and see whether date returns to Nov 14."}
