{"type": "thinking", "text": "Deletion persists; no stale entry from cache. Journal caching seems fine so far. But maybe the cache bug appears with timeline dates or with many entries. Hmm.\n\nLet me look at the broader journal: maybe journal entries include medication log records? The \"journal entry list\" might actually be the list in the Journal tab including previous days. We only have one day.\n\nNow let me think about the changed features and likely injected bugs. This is a QA benchmark with deliberately injected bugs in the changed areas. Likely each changed bullet has a bug. Let me scrutinize each:\n\n1. \"Group editor first-dose picker: a picked value is now compared with the stored one before it is applied.\" — A bug candidate: when picking a first dose from date/time pickers, the app compares with stored value and may fail to apply, e.g., picking an earlier time than start, or picking a time that causes the date to shift. Wait: \"first-dose picker\" might be the START DATE + START TIME? Or perhaps in the group editor there's a \"first dose\" concept: TIMES OF DAY first entry? Hmm.\n\nActually maybe the \"first-dose picker\" is the Time picker for the group start. Bug: picking 2:00 AM auto-shifted start date — that could be the bug from comparing picked vs stored (the night owl logic comparing stored start time to picked). Hmm.\n\n2. \"Journal entry list: loaded entries are now cached in memory between tab switches.\" Bug candidate: duplicate entries or stale entries.\n\n3. \"Medicine list category headers: headings are now generated only for categories holding at least one medicine.\" Bug candidate: header with wrong counts, or a header appearing for an empty category, or all medicines grouped under wrong headers, or headers not shown for archived-only. Let's dig into the medicine list more. Earlier with 2 medicines in 2 categories, headers were correct. But what about ordering, and what if medicines of same category are far apart? Or what if a category has archived meds? Let's test archiving: archive Spironolactone, then check that ANTIANDROGEN header disappears. Also possibly check injecting a medicine with a different preparation form.\n\nAlso, is the header text the category name uppercase — maybe when Custom category, the header should show the custom name. Let's test Custom category medicine.\n\n4. \"Night owl mode ... caption now builds its cut-off text separately from remaining values.\" Bug candidate: caption wrong cutoff, e.g., \"04:00\" vs \"4:00\" formatting, or when start time is 2:00 AM the caption shows \"before 02:00\"? We saw caption constant 04:00. Hmm, maybe the caption should change when night owl is ON vs OFF? It's shown regardless. It's an explanatory caption. Fine.\n\nHmm, maybe the caption has an issue when the times of day include e.g. 11:30 PM: it might display something like \"Doses before 04:00 count as the previous day.\" Something like a wrong value from a different field, e.g., \"Doses before 7:00 AM count as the previous day\" — we saw 04:00 which is likely the constant.\n\nWait, look carefully: the caption element text order: \"Night owl mode\" | \"Doses before 04:00 count as the previous day.\" In the screenshot: \"Night owl mode\" then \"Doses before 04:00 count as the previous day.\" Looks right.\n\nBut what if the caption is supposed to adapt: \"Doses before 11:00 PM count as the previous day\" when start time is 23:00? No.\n\nLet me get back to tangible testing. Plan:\nA. Medicine list: test headers with 3 categories, archive, custom category, and check header counts/labels. Look for wrong grouping/sorting (e.g., a medicine listed under wrong category header).\nB. Group editor: test first-dose picker thoroughly: change start time to earlier/later with night owl off/on, verify preview & saved \"Since\" date. Look for inconsistencies between preview and saved schedule.\nC. Journal: create notes, verify list, cache duplicates maybe with timeline entries.\n\nLet's do medicine list now: go to Plan > Medicines."}
