{"type": "thinking", "text": "The picker opens with 9:00 AM (not 7:00). So the editable value is 9:00. The displayed range's first value 7:00 is something else (maybe start time cached? but start changed to 6:00!). Hmm, maybe it's the \"first dose\" (initial start time 7:00 from the original daily schedule creation) stored separately.\n\nInteresting: this is the \"first-dose\" concept! The group editor has a first-dose time, which was 7:00 AM (the initial TIMES OF DAY when group was created with START TIME 7:00?). Hmm, when I created the group, START TIME was 7:00 and TIMES OF DAY was 7:00. Then I edited start time to 6:00 and time-of-day to 9:00. The weekly row displays \"7:00 AM → 9:00 AM\": maybe it indicates the first dose at 7:00 and regular doses at 9:00? But start time is now 6:00 and the first dose preview is 9:00 on Monday.\n\nHmm, I bet the weekly row is literally showing \"from start time to time\" where \"start time\" is stale due to a bug. But we changed start time to 6:00 via the picker and the row kept 7:00. Unless the row uses the FIRST DOSE time, not the start time.\n\nWait wait. Let me reconsider: maybe the START TIME field is not used at all for the schedule; instead the first dose is determined by the TIMES OF DAY and night owl. And \"first-dose picker\" could be the picker that appears when you tap the TIME row? Hmm.\n\nLet me look at the daily mode again: \"TIMES OF DAY · 1\" with 9:00. The label \"· 1\" is the count = 1. If the weekly row had 2 times, daily would show · 2. So daily and weekly really have separate values? That seems odd for an app design... unless the weekly TIME field is a RANGE (two times) intentionally: maybe weekly mode supports a dose window? Unlikely.\n\nAlternatively — maybe the weekly view's TIME row is displaying the START TIME → dose time as a RANGE because in weekly mode, the group may have multiple times per day (e.g., 7:00 AM and 9:00 AM) and it summarizes as range. The stale 7:00 might come from the daily schedule's ORIGINAL time before edit, because the weekly time list was initialized with both [7:00 existing, 9:00 new].\n\nHmm, but daily showed only 9:00 after switching. Unless switching daily->weekly adds the weekly time 9:00 to the daily list (dedup) and switching weekly->daily rebuilds from daily list...\n\nThis is getting complicated; I should record this observed inconsistency: In Weekly mode, the TIME row shows \"7:00 AM → 9:00 AM\" while Daily mode's TIMES OF DAY shows only \"9:00 AM\". That's a clear cross-view inconsistency. And the picker opens at 9:00 with no way to see/edit 7:00. Also, is the 7:00 dose actually scheduled? Preview shows only 9:00, so 7:00 isn't scheduled — the range display is misleading.\n\nWait, but maybe the range IS the intended display of \"start time → time\" and only weekly shows it. Ugh.\n\nLet me test the earliest behavior: create a NEW group in weekly mode and see what the TIME row shows by default. If it shows \"7:00 AM → 7:00 AM\" that'd be weird. Let me instead cancel this edit and create a fresh group test later.\n\nActually, we still have save/discard tests to do. Let me capture this state to check after save: If I save now (weekly, Mon, time 9:00, start 6:00), then reopen the editor and see whether the TIME row still shows the range. That reveals persistence.\n\nLet me save and observe Plan."}
