{"type": "thinking", "text": "Preserved across daily/weekly switch: \"9:00 AM → 8:00 AM\". So the weekly TIME field has 2 times; the daily TIMES OF DAY has its own 1 time. This looks like a real display bug: the weekly TIME row shows both old and new times after editing (should show only the chosen time). It's reproducible (we did it twice: 7→9 gave 7→9; 9→8 gave 9→8).\n\nBut is this in the changed area? It's the group editor time picker — yes, \"first-dose picker\" (the picker for the first dose time?). Hmm, the TIME row edit might be the \"first-dose picker\".\n\nHowever, maybe this behavior is: the weekly TIME row shows \"first dose → second dose\"? Actually wait, maybe the weekly TIME row is not a range but shows both values because weekly mode supports multiple times per day (like daily), and the display is \"9:00 AM → 8:00 AM\" because... no.\n\nLet me try to determine whether weekly mode supports multiple times: switch to weekly and check if there's an \"Add\" button. No Add. Also the element label is \"TIME\" not \"TIMES OF DAY\". So single.\n\nHmm, but is this a bug introduced by the changed build? The changed bullet says the picker compares picked value with stored before applying. That sounds like: if picked == stored, don't apply (avoid no-op). A bug could be that when different, it appends rather than replaces, or when equal, it appends too.\n\nLet me test the \"same value\" case in weekly mode: tap TIME row, press OK without changing (picked 9:00?). Wait the picker opened at 9:00 previously when the row had 9:00 and 8:00 (the first?). Now the row shows 9:00 → 8:00; which will the picker use? Let me tap and see.\n\nAlso test daily mode: edit the time-of-day from 9:00 to 9:00 (same) and check it doesn't duplicate. And daily edit 9:00→10:00 then see if daily shows 2 times (TIMES OF DAY · 2) — maybe the daily picker correctly replaces.\n\nLet me check daily integrity: in daily mode, tap 9:00 AM row, pick 10:00 AM, OK → does TIMES OF DAY become \"10:00 AM\" only (count 1) or 2? Let's test."}
