n the first dose time (previous) and the new time because the group has TWO doses per selected day? Hmm, no Add button though.\n\nI'm fairly confident this is a bug: \"Editing the weekly TIME leaves the previous time behind, displaying e.g. '9:00 AM → 8:00 AM' and saving the last value instead of the selected sum.\" But is it in the changed area? It is in group scheduling. It might be the injected bug for \"first-dose picker\". Hmm, but the first-dose picker is likely the START time picker.\n\nHold on. Let me reconsider the START date/time. The \"first dose\" might be the START TIME. Consider the bug: \"a picked value is now compared with the stored one before it is applied\" — maybe in the START TIME picker, after picking a new time, the app compares to stored and if different, it applies, but it also shifts the START DATE incorrectly (night owl logic). We saw the shift with 2:00 AM.\n\nLet me carefully test the START TIME picker now with night owl ON/OFF and observe date/preview. Current group: weekly Mon 8:00, start 5:00 AM Nov 14, night owl OFF, daily... Let me test:\nA) Toggle night owl ON. Pick START TIME 2:00 AM. Observe start date & preview.\nB) Then Save and check Plan \"Since\".\n\nLet me do it."}
