{"type": "thinking", "text": "Interesting! Daily mode shows TIMES OF DAY · 1 with 9:00 AM?! The weekly TIME was 8:00 AM. When switching to daily, it shows 9:00 AM. Hmm! Where does 9:00 come from? The daily list probably [9:00] (from earlier daily edit where I set 10:00? wait we set 10:00 earlier, then the group saved as weekly with 8:00, then reopened; daily should maybe show 8:00). It shows 9:00 now — stale from earlier daily state.\n\nSo Daily and Weekly keep separate time lists, and switching modes doesn't synchronize. The saved group uses weekly time (8:00). Daily shows 9:00 (a stale edited value from earlier session). This is a significant consistency bug: the Daily view displays a different dose time (9:00) than the saved schedule (8:00) and Weekly view (8:00).\n\nWait, but maybe the daily list is derived from weekly on load, and after switching it's [9]? Hmm.\n\nLet's check preview: \"9:00 AM Tomorrow\" and \"9:00 AM Nov 16 Mon\" — preview uses 9:00 now! So switching to Daily changed the preview to 9:00. And earlier, when weekly with 8:00, preview showed 8:00 Nov 16 Mon. So the preview reflects the current mode's time list.\n\nWow, so each mode has its own list. That's questionable design but maybe intentional: switching modes preserves separate settings. However the saved group (weekly) shows 8:00; reopening and switching to daily reveals 9:00. Does the daily list affect the saved group after switching? If I save now in daily mode, the group becomes daily with 9:00.\n\nHmm, is this a bug? It might be by design: the editor keeps a daily time list and a weekly time list separately so toggling modes doesn't lose the other's settings. But then showing 9:00 (from an earlier edit) is expected.\n\nLet me test adding a second daily time. Tap \"Add\" (11)."}
