hasizing existing saved group. But before re-filing, let me capture Group 1 with 3 values maybe. Let's reproduce once more cleanly on Group 1 and note that it doesn't happen on a new group.\n\nActually, hmm — maybe there's something else: In Group 1's case, when I opened the edit sheet, the TIME row showed 8:00. I tapped it, and the picker opened at 8:00. I picked 10:00. Then row showed 8→10. In Group 2, row 7:30, picker 7:30, pick 9:30 → 9:30 only. So same flow but different outcome. The difference: Group 1 is existing (loaded from saved state); Group 2 is new.\n\nPossibly the bug: editing an existing group's TIME appends because the weekly schedule is stored as a list and the picker sets the value at index... hmm. Or because the existing group has a \"first dose\" stored (7:00 AM originally), and the weekly row displays firstDose → currentTime when they differ; when editing the time to something different from firstDose, the range shows. In Group 2 (new), there is no stored first dose → no range. And earlier Group 1's range 7→9: the firstDose was 7:00 (original creation time). Then after save, the firstDose likely updated to 9:00 (since range collapsed). Then next edit 9→8: range 9→8 (first dose had become 9). Yes! That matches: the row shows \"firstDose → selectedTime\" when they differ. The firstDose is a separate stored value that only updates on save (or not at all).\n\nWait, but Group 1's start time was 7:00 originally; first dose = 7:00. Then saved group. Reopened, daily time was 9:00 (weekly 8:00?). Hmm, the exact values shifted, but the pattern \"range = firstDose → time\" holds if firstDose updates to the value saved.\n\nLet me test: after saving Group 1 (which currently... we discarded the 8→10 change, so saved state is 8:00), reopen and edit TIME 8:00→10:00: range 8→10 (firstDose 8 = saved weekly time). Yes. So the row displays \"saved first dose time → newly picked time\" whenever they differ. This is likely the actual injected bug: the picker compares the picked value with the stored one before applying, and when they differ it shows/applies both? Hmm.\n\nRegardless, this is reproducible: existing group, edit TIME, pick a different time → row shows \"old → new\". This is the \"first-dose picker\" bug! The field shows the first dose and the new value instead of just the new. The developer couldn't reproduce maybe because they changed the time in Daily mode or created a new group.\n\nLet me be very explicit in the report: The group must already be saved; open Edit group; Weekly; tap TIME; pick a different value; OK. Then the row shows \"8:00 AM → 10:00 AM\".\n\nActually, wait. Let me reconsider: maybe the row \"8:00 AM → 10:00 AM\" is showing a RANGE that is intentional: the first dose (8:00) and the new time (10:00)? That would be weird.\n\nAlso maybe the \"preview\" showing 10:00 confirms the applied value is 10:00; the stale 8:00 display is wrong.\n\nLet me reproduce on Group 1 now with exact steps and confirm the picker's default and the resulting row. Then refile.\n\nDiscard Group 2 first. Since Save is disabled (no meds), just BACK → dialog → Discard."}
