{"type": "thinking", "text": "Now it shows \"11:00 AM → 9:00 AM\": first = 11 (saved), last = 9 (picked). So it's not accumulation from the very first 8; the first is the currently saved value, and it updates on save. So the row shows \"stored → picked\".\n\nThis is likely the injected bug: the compare-with-stored logic keeps the stored value visible alongside the picked one. The developer says \"could not reproduce\" — maybe the reply system is giving generic replies? Or maybe they expect a stronger report with the correct element/quote. Hmm.\n\nMaybe I'm misinterpreting and this range is intended (a common pattern in some apps: show the previous and new time? no).\n\nAlternatively, maybe the intended behavior is that weekly mode supports a dose TIME RANGE (from → to) and the picker sets only one side... but no.\n\nHold on, maybe the row is showing the FIRST DOSE time and the RECURRING time: the group's start time is 5:00 AM, so no. Hmm.\n\nBut wait: The group's \"first dose\" concept could be stored as 11:00 (the saved weekly time) and the \"recurring\" as 9:00 picked. When you change the weekly time, the first dose stays 11:00 deliberately? Then the group would have first dose at 11:00 (today?) and subsequent at 9:00. The PREVIEW shows Nov 16 Mon 9:00 and Nov 23 Mon 9:00 — no 11:00. Hmm, first dose maybe Nov 14 today at 11:00? Preview might not show today because... Let me scroll down to preview in current state: it showed 11:00 earlier. Now let me check preview: if preview shows 11:00 today AND 9:00 Mon, then the range is meaningful: first dose today 11:00, weekly doses 9:00.\n\nWait! Earlier, when I set daily 2 times etc., the preview showed \"9:00 AM Tomorrow, 8:00 PM Tomorrow, ...\" with start at 2:00. The preview picks future dose times from start. If the weekly first dose is 11:00 today (saved), and recurring time 9:00 Monday... the preview would show 11:00 today then 9:00 Nov 16. Let me check.\n\nActually earlier with 8→11, the preview (before save) showed only 10:00 Nov 16/23 (in an earlier instance). Hmm, but that was with start 5:00 and Mon only; today is Sat, so first dose would be Nov 16. If first dose 8:00 is stored as a \"one-time first dose\" on start date... The preview would show Nov 16 at 8:00 plus Nov 16 at 11? It didn't.\n\nLet me scroll and look now."}
