{"type": "thinking", "text": "Now switch to Weekly and change the time to 9:00, then Save. Then reopen and edit another time; see if range appears.\n\nActually to mirror Group 1's history: Group 1 was created in Daily (7:00), saved as Daily, then reopened and switched to Weekly, edited to 9:00, saved. Then later edits showed ranges. For Group 2: create Daily 7:30, save. Then reopen, switch to Weekly, edit 9:00, save. Then reopen, edit TIME 10:00 → see if \"9:00 → 10:00\".\n\nThat's a longer sequence but likely the true repro. But my last repro: Group 1 saved weekly, reopened, edited TIME, immediately showed range. Group 1 had history. Hmm, maybe the range appears only when the group has previous weekly schedule data with a different time. Since Group 1 was saved weekly with 11:00 and I edited to 9:00, the row showed 11→9 — consistent with \"saved → picked\".\n\nFor Group 2, after saving weekly with 9:00, reopen and edit to 10:00: if the row shows 9→10, then it's simply \"saved group\" behavior (which Group 2 new-unsaved didn't show).\n\nLet's just do it: switch to weekly now (time 7:30), pick 9:00, save. Then reopen, edit time to 10:00, observe.\n\nActually simpler: switch to weekly now, pick 9:00, save directly (without intermediate save). Then reopen and edit 9→10.\n\nSteps: tap Weekly (10)."}
