s: a start and an end (a range), i.e., the week's timeframe. The pickers: first time sets the range start, second time sets the range end. That would mean the TIME field is a \"time window\" for the weekly dose. But PREVIEW showing only 10:30 contradicts.\n\nI'm confident this is a bug. But the developer rejected twice. Maybe I should report the underlying wrong behavior differently: \"The TIME row keeps showing the previously stored session's time after picking a new one\" — but that's the same.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the correct bug is that the app saves the NEW value but the row displays stale old value → yes.\n\nLet me refile with explicit save-then-edit steps and mention it happens only for saved groups.\n\nActually, wait. Maybe the issue is that the app runs the comparison \"picked value vs stored\" and, when they differ, appends to the times list — that's precisely the changed bullet. The developer may have tried a NEW group (where stored == default and the picked differs... hmm, in the new group it replaced). So maybe the code path: for a saved group, the list has a \"synced\" state; the picker adds a new entry. Whatever.\n\nLet me refile with the exact verification of the saved state and the Plan card. I'll also mention the saved result is 10:30 (the second value). Steps:\n1. Create a group, add medicine, weekly, save (Plan card shows \"Every week · Sat · 9:30 AM\").\n2. Tap the saved group card → Edit group (Weekly).\n3. Tap TIME row (9:30 AM) → pick 10:30 AM → OK.\n4. TIME row now shows \"9:30 AM → 10:30 AM\".\n5. Save → Plan card shows 10:30 AM, but the editor had displayed two times.\n\nLet me discard current edits first (to preserve Group 2 as 9:30). Then maybe delete Group 2 to clean up? There may be a delete option in the group editor (DANGER ZONE?). Let me check the group editor bottom for delete. Earlier in the creation view, the sheet was cut off. Let me scroll to the bottom in the edit group view. There might be \"Delete group\". We'll clean up later.\n\nDiscard now."}
