ic state.\n\nLet me focus on the night owl caption. The caption says \"Doses before 04:00 count as the previous day.\" Maybe the intended behavior: the cutoff should be derived from the first dose? Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe the caption includes the cut-off time formatted from a value; if the value is stored as a time in minutes and formatted elsewhere, a bug might show \"Doses before 04:00 count as the previous day.\" vs \"Doses before 4:00 AM...\" — I can't know.\n\nLet's test toggling night owl and observe PREVIEW dates for a 2:00 AM dose. That could reveal whether the caption's claim matches behavior. Set daily time to 2:00 AM with night owl ON; preview should show the dose counted as previous day (date label one day earlier) — maybe the preview would show \"Today\" for tomorrow's 2 AM dose. If the caption says \"before 04:00 counts as previous day\" but the preview shows the next day's date, the behavior contradicts the caption → bug.\n\nBut the caption text may be fine; the bug might be in the preview or schedule logic. The changed bullet is caption text only though.\n\nHmm, let me look at the caption in another state: when night owl is ON and the first dose is after midnight (2:00 AM), maybe the caption should say \"Doses before 04:00 count as the previous day.\" — same. OK.\n\nMaybe the caption bug is a formatting issue where the cut-off \"04:00\" is rendered as the raw enum value or something. It looked fine.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the caption's cut-off should be \"04:00\" but shows \"04:00\" only for one locale. Fine.\n\nLet me look at the START TIME title's \"After midnight\" label: when start time is after midnight (< 04:00), the label \"After midnight\" is shown next to START TIME. This is a different feature. Hmm.\n\nMaybe the night owl caption's cutoff is supposed to be dynamic: the cutoff is set based on the group's \"night owl cutoff\" which might default to 04:00. Not user-editable.\n\nI suspect the injected bug for night owl could be: the caption is shown even when night owl is OFF (it's explanatory, so fine), OR the caption disappears when enabled. We saw it stays.\n\nHmm, wait. Maybe the caption's cut-off value should reflect the *night owl cutoff*, which might be configurable in Settings. The caption uses \"04:00\" hardcoded. If Settings has a night owl cutoff option, the caption might not update. Let me check Settings for night owl. Good idea: check Settings for any related setting."}
