unt as the previous day.\" Hmm.\n\nLet me test the night owl preview semantics: with night owl ON and dose at 2:00 AM, what does PREVIEW show? If the caption claims 2 AM counts as previous day, then the preview for a 2:00 AM dose tomorrow should be labeled with today's date (or \"Today\"). Let's test and see if the preview/Plan behavior is consistent with the caption. If it's inconsistent, maybe the injected bug (though the bullet is about caption text).\n\nTest setup: Group 2 weekly Sat 9:30. Switch Daily, set time 2:00 AM, night owl ON, start time default (or set to 2:00). Then check PREVIEW. Hmm, this changes Group 2 temporarily; I'll discard after.\n\nActually, let me use Group 2 and test:\n1. Edit Group 2.\n2. Switch Daily.\n3. Set first time 2:00 AM (or add and remove).\n4. Night owl ON.\n5. Check preview labels.\n\nBut the preview labels show \"Today/Tomorrow/Nov 21 Sat\" based on date. With night owl, a 2 AM dose on Nov 15 might display as \"Today\" (Nov 14) — that's the intended behavior. If it shows \"Tomorrow\", the night owl logic isn't applied even though the caption says so.\n\nThis tests the feature's actual behavior; the changed bullet is just the caption though. Still, a mismatch between caption and behavior would be a bug.\n\nLet me do it. Go to Plan → Group 2 → Daily → edit time to 2:00 AM → night owl ON → check preview.\n\nCurrently on Settings; go Plan."}
