t notes. Let me add a timeline date and see the Journal. Actually the TIMELINE card on Journal: \"Add a date\" navigates to the Timeline screen with a sheet. Adding a date likely shows it in TIMELINE card? Let's explore the journal/timeline and see if entries (dates) appear and cache.\n\nAlso, maybe the \"journal entry list\" includes medication logs? No.\n\nLet me look at the Journal tab again and add a date. Journal → TIMELINE \"Add a date\". We tapped it before and got a sheet \"Add a date\" with Name/Date/Icon/Color/Pin/Save, then Cancel returned to the Timeline screen. So the Journal's \"Add a date\" opens the Timeline screen with a sheet. Let's add a date now: name \"Started HRT\", date Nov 14, icon Event, save. Then check Journal TIMELINE card and caching across tabs."}
