{"type": "thinking", "text": "One note. The journal list has one entry. Maybe journal entries only one per day. So to test cache with multiple entries, I'd need entries on other days. Hmm, can I create a note for a different day? Perhaps the note's date row (Today Nov 14 Sat) is clickable but disabled. What if I add a timeline date for another day? No.\n\nAlternatively, maybe notes can be added via Home quick action? Home has \"Add medication log record\" only.\n\nMaybe the \"journal entry list\" refers to a different screen: perhaps the Journal tab shows the notes list and also a list of timeline dates, and the caching refers to both.\n\nHmm. Let me test the cache in another way: entries loaded in Journal, then data changes elsewhere (e.g., adding a timeline date from the Timeline screen), then return to Journal — is the timeline card updated or stale? We added the date while in the Timeline screen and returning to Journal showed it (fresh). Now if we return from another tab, cache may show.\n\nAnother idea: the cache bug could be that the Journal list doesn't refresh when the date changes (midnight) — untestable.\n\nLet me look at the Journal screen now and switch tabs a few times to see duplicates/bugs.\n\nActually, maybe the cache bug is about entries being *appended* each time the tab is revisited — with one note we'd see 2 cards. We didn't see duplicates. Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe the journal entry list refers to the list of notes under NOTES, and each entry displayed as a card. With one note, no duplicates seen. Let's now check the note's content after tab switches: \"Entry one\" — good.\n\nLet me try a more exotic flow: while editing a note, switch tabs (bottom nav) mid-edit? The editor is inline; tapping Plan while the keyboard is up might switch tabs and keep the draft? Then returning might show the draft or saved state. Could reveal caching issues. But risky.\n\nMaybe I should look at the \"LAST 30 DAYS\" filter again: it's clickable but does nothing visible. Perhaps tapping it should open a menu to change the range, and with the new caching the list doesn't update. Let me tap it now (with a note present) and see."}
