{"type": "thinking", "text": "Editing a timeline date gives Edit date sheet with Delete/Save. No notes.\n\nSince I can't create multiple notes easily, maybe I can change the device date? Not allowed via tools. Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe the journal notes list includes a note per day, and one can only write for today. The cache bug might be about the TIMELINE LIST (\"journal entry list\" could refer to the timeline dates list). We added a date and the Journal card updated. Switching tabs kept. Hmm.\n\nHold on — maybe the \"journal entry list\" is the ALL DATES list on the Timeline screen, and the \"loaded entries are cached in memory between tab switches\" means when you add a date, switch to another tab, and come back, the list might be duplicated or stale. Let's test:\n- On Timeline screen (2 dates), switch to Plan tab, then back to Journal; the Journal card shows timeline. Then open Timeline screen — are dates duplicated?\n- Also, adding a date while the cache holds an old list could result in a stale list (missing new date) after tab switching.\n\nLet me test the stale scenario: Currently the Timeline screen loaded with 2 dates. Go to Journal tab? Actually the Timeline screen is a separate route (not a tab). The bottom nav isn't visible on the Timeline screen. So tab switching isn't possible from there.\n\nHmm.\n\nLet me step back and think about the injected bug for \"Journal entry list: loaded entries are now cached in memory between tab switches.\" A classic injected bug: the cache is keyed incorrectly or the list is not cleared, causing duplicates or stale ordering. Another classic: when switching tabs, the cached entries are re-added to the list → duplicated entries. With one note, duplicates would show 2 cards, which we did NOT see. Unless duplicates only appear when revisiting via a different route (e.g., from Journal via Home tab then Journal).\n\nWe switched Plan→Journal twice; no duplicates. Hmm.\n\nWhat about switching from the Journal tab to Home and back multiple times? Same thing.\n\nMaybe the cache bug is that notes are cached but the \"No earlier notes\" state is wrong: e.g., the cache returns the entries but the list shows them under the wrong date group. Not visible with today only.\n\nAlternatively, maybe there is a \"journal entries\" list elsewhere — e.g., \"Open history\" on Plan? That's medication history. Hmm, \"journal\" might include the \"Open history\" screen. Let me check Plan > Open history (881,148). That could be the \"journal entry list\" of dose records! Let's look."}
