{"type": "thinking", "text": "History screen shows calendar and \"NOVEMBER RECORDS / No records yet.\" 0 records logged. Fine.\n\nLet's go back to Journal and try to think about the cache more. Maybe the \"journal entry list\" refers to this history's records list — but with no logs, can't test.\n\nHmm, maybe I should log a dose to populate records. There's a dose record card at Plan for today (Group 2 at 9:30). We could log it (tap the record card). Then History has 1 record. The journal caching bullet might refer to the journal notes, not records.\n\nLet me step back and consider what other bugs might be intentionally injected. The four changed bullets suggest four potential bug locations. I've found a suspicious weekly TIME range (maybe unrelated). Let me examine each bullet more carefully with fresh eyes:\n\n1. \"Group editor first-dose picker: a picked value is now compared with the stored one before it is applied.\"\nMaybe the \"first-dose picker\" is the START TIME picker. Let's test: change START TIME to a time EARLIER than the current TIMES OF DAY, then check the PREVIEW. We saw weird transitions. Specifically, with Group 2: start 7:03 AM, weekly Sat 9:30. Preview shows \"10:30 Today\"? Wait, earlier preview showed \"10:30 AM Today, 10:30 AM Nov 21\". Hmm, that was after picking 10:30. So first dose today 10:30 — fine.\n\nLet's test: set START TIME to 11:00 AM (after the 9:30 dose today). Then preview should skip today's 9:30 and show next Saturday. And the group's \"Since\" would be Nov 14 still.\n\nThen set START TIME back to 7:00.\n\nMaybe the bug: when picking a start time later than today's dose time, the PREVIEW still shows today's dose (doesn't apply), i.e., the comparison logic fails to apply the new time. That would match \"picked value compared with stored one before applied\"! Let's test: In Group 2 (weekly Sat 9:30, start 7:03), PREVIEW shows \"9:30 AM Today\"? Let's check current: earlier preview showed \"10:30 AM Today\" when time picked 10:30. Now cancelled. Let's open editor, scroll to preview to see 9:30 Today, then change START TIME to 11:00 and see if preview updates to next Sat (or erroneously still Today).\n\nDo that now. Go back to Journal? We're on History; back twice? Actually from Plan → Open history. Press back to Plan."}
