{"type": "thinking", "text": "Whoa, significant! After picking START DATE Nov 10 (a past date), the START TIME changed to \"12:00 AM\" (from 11:00 AM), and a \"PAST SCHEDULE\" section appeared with options Mark as completed / Mark as missed / Hide. Also DAYS OF WEEK now has Tuesday checked (was Saturday) — it auto-selected Tuesday (the weekday of Nov 10) and unchecked Saturday! That's expected maybe (start date's weekday). And TIME is 9:30 (weekly).\n\nThe START TIME became 12:00 AM. Is that a bug? Changing the start DATE reset the START TIME to 12:00 AM. That seems like a bug: the user picked a date, and the time field lost 11:00 AM, replaced with 12:00 AM.\n\nHmm, but maybe the app sets time to midnight when the start date is in the past to mark the past schedule? Hmm, the \"PAST SCHEDULE\" section appeared because start date is in the past. Maybe the app sets the start time to 12:00 AM so the first schedule occurrence is on Nov 10? No...\n\nLet's think: before, start date Nov 14 (today), start time 11:00 AM. After picking Nov 10 date, time becomes 12:00 AM. That's a reset of the time. Could be the \"first-dose picker\" bug: picking a new date causes the stored time to be compared/reset. This might be the injected bug! \"Group editor first-dose picker: a picked value is now compared with the stored one before it is applied.\" Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe the START TIME \"12:00 AM\" is the default time for the first dose on the newly selected date (since 11:00 AM Nov 10 is in the past, maybe it clamps?). Hmm, why 12:00 AM? If the date is in the past, maybe the time is set to 12:00 AM as a placeholder.\n\nLet me test the reverse: pick START DATE Nov 20 (future) and see if START TIME resets to 12:00 AM too. If yes, then changing date always resets the time — a bug?\n\nActually wait — maybe the date picker's \"OK\" resets the time because the picked datetime (Nov 10 11:00) is in the past and the app normalizes to midnight? Hmm.\n\nLet me test with a future date (Nov 20). Tap START DATE (2), pick Nov 20, OK."}
